  "prefLabel": "Ret 201.10 Modification or Suspension of Rules",
  "priorExpiration": "2001-04-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ret 201.10 Modification or Suspension of Rules. The presiding officer or, upon reviewing a presiding officer's recommendation pursuant to Ret 204.09 below, the board of trustees shall modify or suspend any requirement or limitation imposed by this chapter in the interest of justice except those which are also mandated by statute. Such modification or suspension may be made on the presiding officer's or the board's own initiative or upon the filing of a motion by any party or intervenor.\n\nSource. #5880, eff 8-19-94, EXPIRED: 8-19-00\n\nNew. #7374, INTERIM, eff 10-13-00, EXPIRES: 4-11-01; ss by #7477, eff 4-10-01; ss by #7572, eff 10-10-01; ss by #12709, eff 1-9-19",
